payload/webos25/  --  webOS-25 (C5-class) decoder-inject payload
=================================================================

Profile: webos25-armel-gst124   (VERIFIED mechanism -- see ../../README.md)

Drop the two cross-built ARM soft-float (armel, EABI5) binaries HERE before
packaging the .ipk:

    payload/webos25/libgstdtsdec.so     patched dtsdec (gst-plugins-bad 1.22,
                                        sink caps widened to also accept
                                        audio/x-unknown, codec-id=A_DTS), with
                                        FFmpeg n4.4.4's dca decoder linked in
                                        statically (DTS core, DTS-HD MA/HRA,
                                        DTS Express; up to 7.1, S32LE)
    payload/webos25/libgstadecswitch.so same-family stream-switch bin

Where they come from
--------------------
They are the committed, on-device-verified binaries in webos25/restore/:

    cp ../../../restore/out/libgstdtsdec.so \
       ../../../restore/switch-out/libgstadecswitch.so  .

(rebuild with restore/build.sh and restore/build-switch.sh; see RELEASING.md).

At enable time the JS service copies both to /var/lib/webosbrew/dts25/, then
regenerates the media GStreamer registry including dtsdec. libgstdtsdec.so
needs nothing but GStreamer, GLib and libc from the TV: no bundled library and
no RPATH. (Builds before webos25-2.43 also shipped libdca.so.0 into
/var/lib/webosbrew/dts25/libs/; a copy left there is unused.)

ABI constraints (must hold or the plugin will not load on the C5)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
  - 32-bit ARM, EABI5 soft-float  (loader ld-linux.so.3, e_flags 0x05000200)
  - max referenced GLIBC symbol <= 2.35  (TV has glibc 2.35)
  - GStreamer 1.22 plugin ABI (loads in the TV's 1.24 -- verified on-device)

These .so files are NOT committed here (see ../../.gitignore). They are
LGPL-2.1-or-later; ship ../../licenses/ (NOTICE.md has the source offer) with
any distributed .ipk.
